2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/83/79/f5/1e/5344483efbb862ef/sonne_familien_original.jpg?hash=d438c75ef926db096f82ccc08bc06dcdab6145218de50ab0b7f5fe328dfbe4e6.1794988799
2 FORM jpg
2 NOTE https://danishimmigrants.weebly.com/familien-sonne-fra-nexoslash.html
3 CONT
3 CONT The characters. Front row from left:
3 CONT The angry boy in matrostøj is Erik Sonne, my father, and the only son of the silver bride couple.
3 CONT The lady beside him is Blanche Sonne, with daughter, Marie-Térèse, French, from Buenos Aires, Argentina, married to Thyge Sonne, brother of Harmen.
3 CONT Then comes the testimony Sonne and then the silver bride couple.
3 CONT The sitting boy in matrostøj is Aage Kofoed, son of Rudolf Kofoed and Thora Sonne. He suffered from childbirth (polio) and died a few years later.
3 CONT
3 CONT Second row:
3 CONT Behind Erik Sonne is his two sisters, Inger, later married Bierrie and residing in New York, and Karen later married Kiaer and resided in London. Then Tyge Sonne from Argentina and Eriks third sister, Gerda, later married Rist, an
3 CONC d resided in Copenhagen.
3 CONT Then see Thora Sonne, later married Tillisch, Øbjerggaard.
3 CONT Behind her is Rudolf Kofoed, Director of Old Carlsberg (his mother was born Rothe) and then
3 CONT Christian Sonne, brother of Harmen and Thyge, a well-known farmer and politician.
3 CONT The two ladies are Christian Sonnes wife Sofie, born Güttig, German from Flensburg, and
3 CONT Thora Kofoed, married to Rudolf Kofoed, born Sonne, and only daughter of probationist Sonne. Behind Thyge Sonne ses
3 CONT Hans Georg Kofoed, son of Rudolf and Thora Kofoed.
3 CONT
3 CONT Top row:
3 CONT Behind Hans Georg Kofoed is his sister Ella Kofoed. Then comes
3 CONT August Sonne, later judge in Køge, son of Christian and Sofie Sonne.
3 CONT Next comes Harmen, Christian and Thyges youngest brother,
3 CONT August Sonne, later a well-known doctor in Vejle.
3 CONT Then another Argentine, Robert Sonne, son of Thyge and Blanche, and then two sons of Christian and Sofie Sonne:
3 CONT Hans Sonne, later banker in New York and
3 CONT Henry Sonne, his brother.
3 CONT
3 CONT Written by the son of the silver brothers, Harmen Sonne.
